   "failure_scenario": "An operator retries deployment after an interruption, but an incomplete service inspection is mistaken for confirmation that the executor stopped, allowing the checkout to change while it remains running. Similar inspection failures can cause installation to replace its plist or uninstallation to delete it without stopping the executor.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "bun \"$TMPDIR/f1-adjudicate.ts\"",
    "output": "Throwaway script imported HEAD's service module and exercised its public functions with temporary plists and fake command runners; no real launchctl or network calls.\nRecovery, missing-service message with exit 1: checkoutNext=true, bootout=false, executorStillLoaded=true.\nRecovery, missing-service message with exit null: checkoutNext=true, bootout=false, executorStillLoaded=true.\nRecovery, missing-service message with exit 113 and timedOut=true: checkoutNext=true, bootout=false, executorStillLoaded=true.\nReconciliation, exit 0 and timedOut=true: error=false, intentGone=true, bootstrap=false.\nInstall collision inspection, permission error: oldStopped=true, oldPlistRemovedBeforeEnable=true; installation subsequently failed.\nUninstall, permission error: error=false, plistDeleted=true, executorStillLoaded=true.\nStatus, permission error: custom.executor: not loaded."
   },
   "evidence": "HEAD service.ts:325 accepts `if (result.exitCode === 0) return true;` without checking timedOut. Lines 326\u2013331 return false when stderr contains the missing-service line, regardless of exit status or timeout. Shutdown therefore skips bootout for malformed absence results, and reconciliation can accept a timed-out success. Install's separate predicate at line 421 checks only `exitCode === 0`; its collision guard at line 514 consequently permits mutation after unknown inspections. Uninstall uses the equivalent predicate at lines 148\u2013149 before unconditionally deleting the plist at line 578. Status at line 965 maps every nonzero result to `not loaded`. Base already contained these latter predicates, but did not recognize executor units or contain the new executor recovery/reconciliation helper; the primary defect is introduced, with the legacy predicates newly exposed to executors. After completing HEAD probes, inspection of the later diff showed a shared inspectService that requires non-timed-out exit 0 for loaded, or non-timed-out exit 113 with the domain-specific missing-service line for absent. Other results become unknown; executor control, install, uninstall and status all use it."
  },
  "B": {
   "verdict": "REAL",
   "failure_scenario": "A deploy recovers from an interrupted rollback, and its 'is the executor loaded?' query to launchctl fails in an abnormal way: it is killed by a signal or exits with a status other than 'not found', yet its error text still reads 'Could not find service'. The deploy treats the executor as stopped, disables it and checks out the new release without ever confirming that the executor was unloaded. The same lenient handling of failed queries, already present at base, now also covers the executor in install's label-collision check, uninstall and status.",
   "reproduction": {
    "command": "Copied test/deploy.test.ts to $TMPDIR, rewrote its relative imports to absolute paths and appended a test. It writes a 'rollback' intent, makes the fake 'launchctl print' return the exact missing-service message with either exitCode null (killed by a signal) or exitCode 1, and also tries exitCode 0 with timedOut true. It then runs deploy(7400, 'feature', false, {executor: true}) and runs only these tests with `bun test $D/repro.test.ts -t REPRO`.",
    "output": "RESULT signal error: ok\nCALLS signal [\"launchctl print gui/501/custom.gate-executor\",\"launchctl disable ...\",\"git checkout -q --detach next\",\"launchctl enable ...\",\"launchctl print ...\",\"launchctl bootstrap ...\"]\nRESULT exit1 error: ok\nCALLS exit1 [same sequence, including git checkout -q --detach next]\nRESULT timeout0 error: Executor custom.gate-executor shutdown unconfirmed: Error: agent still loaded ... (fails safe in shutdown)\n3 pass"
   },
   "evidence": "At head, executorControl.isLoaded (src/cli/service.ts:322-335) is: `if (result.exitCode === 0) return true; if (result.stderr.split(\"\\n\").includes(`Could not find service \"${unit.label}\" in domain for user gui: ${uid}`)) return false; throw ...`. It never checks `timedOut`, and it accepts the missing-service message whatever the exit status, including null. sh() returns `timedOut` with allowFail (proc.ts:1205-1220). Install's own isLoaded (line 421, `exitCode === 0`), uninstall's loaded() (lines 148, 577) and status (line 965, `exitCode === 0 ? \"loaded\" : \"not loaded\"`) are identical at base (base lines 318, 147, 811), but they now also handle the executor unit. Severity is minor because real launchctl only prints that message with exit 113 when the service is absent. The bypass needs launchctl to be killed or time out after printing that exact message, or a permission error on the user's own gui domain. In the shutdown path, exit 0 with timedOut fails safe. In reconcile it would skip bootstrap and report success."
